# Root build context for the container images (api + migrate job, web,
# browser-worker). Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps
# host artifacts and secrets out of the daemon: `node_modules`, `.next`,
# `dist` and `.turbo` are all rebuilt inside the image from the lockfile, and
# `.env*` files are runtime inputs (compose `env_file`), never build inputs.
#
# `.env.staging.example` / `.env.example` are intentionally NOT ignored: they
# hold placeholders only and document the contract the image expects.
.git
.gitignore
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/coverage
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.staging.example
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
deploy/staging/docker-compose.staging.yml
README.md
**/*.md
docs/
db/tests/
db/seeds/